⚠️ severity: IMPORTANT —
⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the per-ref concurrency group collapses all default-ref dispatch lanes into one global queue**

`ai-teammate-ref-{github.ref}` is correct for head-ref dispatches (`workflowRef={branch}` → per-branch serialization — the gh-1540 goal, well tested). But every lane that dispatches at a **non-branch ref** now shares the single group `ai-teammate-ref-refs/heads/main`:

- **Fork-PR legs** reroute onto `BASE_MACHINE_REF = 'main'` (`js/common/forkDispatch.js:33`) — every cross-repo PR leg, any ticket;
- **`review-external-once`** (`sm_github.json`) has no `workflowRef` → default ref — external PR reviews;
- **`dev-on-assignment`** (the SM dev re-derive safety net) — same;
- manual UI dispatches with no inputs (the old expression's `github.run_id` escape hatch is gone).

Before this change those keyed per-anchor (`ai-teammate-<issue>` / `ai-teammate-pr-<N>`) and ran in parallel across unrelated work. The deleted test asserted exactly this guarantee — *"concurrency group keeps PR-anchored runs per-PR … must not share one global group"* (the #544 lesson, whose explanatory comment this diff also removes). Concrete cost: a wave of external PRs (the rule's own docs: "the trio drains over consecutive ticks") now reviews strictly one-at-a-time **globally**, ~17 min per leg, and fork legs queue behind them.

Secondary: an `assigned`-event run and a same-issue dispatch run previously shared `ai-teammate-<issue>`; the new expression splits them, so the cross-trigger-type pair no longer serializes (re-opening the run-list-probe lag window there).

**Fix**: key dispatch runs on the resolved item branch rather than the dispatch ref — e.g. have the SM pass `inputs.branch` and group on `github.event.inputs.branch || format('issue-{0}', github.event.inputs.issue) || github.ref`. Same-head lanes still collide into one group (the gh-1540 goal), while unrelated branches and branch-less issue legs keep their own groups. Please also add a template test pinning "unrelated PRs do not share a group" — the guarantee the old test carried.
